  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Determination\\n\\nWhen a stored observation cursor is rejected, this workspace's integration should expect **Ordarium's `InvalidCursorError` — code `INVALID_CURSOR`**, failing closed:\\n\\n> `\\\"The change cursor is not a valid durable position; refusing to guess a resume point\\\"`\\n\\nIt is **not** `LEDGER_CORRUPT`/`LedgerCorruptError` and it is **not** a silent restart from the beginning of the feed.\\n\\nTrigger: the consumer passes back a durable position (the `cursor` from `StateChangePage`) that either cannot be decoded or exceeds the ledger's **global high-water mark** — e.g. after the ledger was restored/replaced, which lowers the mark.\\n\\n## The conflicting sources\\n\\n`docs/engineering/09-error-contract-a.md` and `09-error-contract-b.md` both claim \\\"normative, current scope\\\", and disagree:\\n\\n- **A**: the contract is **global** — one position shared by all readers of the store.\\n- **B**: the contract is **per-consumer** — each consumer holds its own independent position.\\n\\nNeither is listed in `docs/engineering/README.md`, neither is dated, and neither cites a supersession. So the tiebreak is not local doc precedence — it is the **pinned dependency artifact**, which owns thi",
